Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the alcor driver writing data before the associated MMC command had completed. This occurred because the driver was set up to trigger data transfer immediately after submitting the command, without waiting for the CMD_END interrupt. In some cases, the interrupt indicated that the hardware was ready to write data (WRITE_BUF_RDY) while the command was still in progress, leading to data CRC errors and write failures. Additionally, the function responsible for triggering data transfer was called multiple times unnecessarily, which added to the confusion and potential for errors.

